---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Invitation from '../components/Invitation.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Alastair Brayne | AI consultant, founder & engineer"
  description="Meet Alastair Brayne: 20+ years in software and CTO roles, an AI startup founder and trained psychotherapist. Fractional and contract AI consultancy through ExFu."
>
  <section class="page-hero about-hero">
    <div class="wrap about-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow red">Hello. I’m Alastair.</p><h1>
          People.<br />Technology.<br />Getting it done.
        </h1><p class="lead">
          I help people turn the possibilities of AI into something useful in their work. ExFu is
          where I bring together experience in business, engineering and working with people.
        </p><a class="text-link" href="/enquire/"
          >Tell me what you’re working on <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </div><figure class="headshot">
        <img
          src="/images/alastair-headshot.jpg"
          alt="Alastair Brayne outdoors"
          width="840"
          height="840"
          fetchpriority="high"
        /><figcaption>Alastair Brayne · Bristol, UK</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="wrap reading-layout section">
    <nav class="contents" aria-label="On this page">
      <p>On this page</p><a href="#approach">How I approach the work</a><a href="#experience"
        >Experience & CVs</a
      ><a href="#tools">Tools out in the open</a><a href="#working">Working together</a>
    </nav><div class="prose">
      <section id="approach">
        <h2>The work has to make sense for the people doing it.</h2><p class="lead">
          A good technical idea is only part of a useful implementation.
        </p><p>
          There is also the question of what the business needs, who will use the result, and what
          it will take to keep it working. I bring those questions into the room with the
          engineering.
        </p><p>
          I have spent more than 20 years building software and leading technical work, including as
          a CTO. Running an AI-enabled product startup has also meant making the decisions about
          what to prioritise, what to test, and where to spend limited time.
        </p><p>
          Alongside that, I retrained as a psychotherapist. It informs how I listen, how I support
          someone learning an unfamiliar tool, and how I think about change inside a team. In ExFu
          engagements, the work is AI consultancy.
        </p><p>
          I’m particularly interested in applications that make room for useful work nobody
          currently has the capacity to do. That might be exploring a revenue opportunity,
          connecting knowledge across a business, or supporting someone with the admin that keeps
          piling up.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="experience">
        <h2>Experience you can look into.</h2><div class="experience-list">
          <div>
            <h3>Software engineering & technical leadership</h3><p>
              More than two decades of full-stack development and technical leadership, including
              CTO work. Enough hands-on experience to move between the business question and the
              implementation.
            </p>
          </div><div>
            <h3>AI product & consultancy</h3><p>
              Five years building an LLM-enabled product startup, alongside consultancy across
              personal agent setup, internal AI work and customer-facing agents. Recent engagements
              include travel and EV mapping businesses.
            </p>
          </div><div>
            <h3>People & psychology</h3><p>
              A background in AI and psychology, followed by psychotherapy training. An interest in
              how people think, learn and work runs through what I do.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div><div class="download-links">
          <a href="/downloads/alastair-brayne-commercial-cv.pdf">Commercial CV <span>PDF ↗</span></a
          ><a href="/downloads/alastair-brayne-technical-cv.pdf">Technical CV <span>PDF ↗</span></a>
        </div><p>
          For more detail, <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/albrayne">find me on LinkedIn</a> or read
          the <a href="/fractional-support/#recent-experience">recent project accounts</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="tools">
        <h2>Some of the tools are out in the open.</h2><p>
          I build and share agent tooling through the ExFu marketplace. It includes approaches to
          managing context, planning work and recording the decisions agents make along the way.
        </p><p>
          That is also how this website was developed: human direction, agent implementation, and a
          record of what was chosen and why.
        </p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/exfu/exfu-marketplace"
          >Explore the ExFu marketplace <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </section>
      <section id="working">
        <h2>Working together.</h2><p>
          I take on fractional and contract engagements, with remote work preferred. I’m based in
          Bristol and can arrange in-person sessions around the calendar.
        </p><p>
          If you are a founder, a CTO, an internal advocate or a recruiter with a suitable brief,
          I’d be glad to hear what you are trying to move forward. If you are looking for help with
          your own workload, <a href="/personal-support/">personal support</a> may be the right place
          to start.
        </p><p>ExFu is my AI consultancy and tooling brand, operated by WhaleyBear Ltd.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
  <Invitation />
</Layout>
